/**
 * A program that builds `rulesets.probe_missing` and computes nothing, so the index can be asked
 * about it: four of the five scalar primitives are filed and `/` is not.
 *
 * Today this is the whole reading. A replacement that walks a function and meets `x / w` would have
 * to refuse at that node, and that red cannot be shown yet: there is no `reinterp` to write it
 * with, so the only red available is the index saying `no rule` -- which is a statement about the
 * ruleset, not about a replacement. The case next to this one pins that, and says so.
 */
import rulesets.probe_missing

func main(): int sync {
    println(1)
    return 0
}